{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547347-strangest-convergence","id":1547347,"title":"Strangest Convergence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-30T16:17:23-08:00","id":1547347,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Strangest Convergence","content":"So, does anyone know of any event, circumstance, scenario or anything like that that could bring together several unrelated kindreds to the same city, at the same time? Let it be clear that most of them do not know each other, they can appear alone or in groups, also there is no specificity of clan or generation. It is as chaotic as it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T16:29:51-08:00","id":1547350,"title":"","content":"The easiest offer on the table is probably to refer to &quot;fate&quot; or &quot;fortune&quot; and leave it at that. It is the World of Darkness after all so things being affected by supernatural forces seems very much in character.<br /> <br /> Or you can provide individual reasons and circumstances that leads them to go to that city. If someone asks about it you can make a hint or reference to the Jyhad and the manipulation of ancient Kindred from the shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T17:35:51-08:00","id":1547353,"title":"","content":"The most common ones I can think of are either political or social events. If there is a Conclave, it's practically a given that a lot of retinue or onlookers arrive with the bigwigs. Same if someone important throws some kind of party (a ball, rave, celebration or whatever) which functions as a chance to be seen and see others.<br /> <br /> There are a few examples of vampires converging in a city because they have been 'called' there - not necessarily by a Discipline power, sometimes a supernatural presence can do the same. You can be pretty hand-wavy with that one and make the source whatever your plot demands: a celestial event, an elder in torpor, a magic ritual gone wrong.. or something tugging the strings of fate, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> mentioned. It's probably best to tie it somehow in with how you plan the story to unfold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T17:37:49-08:00","id":1547354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547347-strangest-convergence#post1547347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does anyone know of any event, circumstance, scenario or anything like that that could bring together several unrelated kindreds to the same city, at the same time? Let it be clear that most of them do not know each other, they can appear alone or in groups, also there is no specificity of clan or generation. It is as chaotic as it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>War is probably your best bet.<br /> <br /> Conflict makes humans band together despite their differences to take on a common enemy. As long as everyone can agree that the threat is great enough and that the only option is to fight, then a pacifist bookworm, a doctor, a CEO, and a 1% biker will all meet up and work together.<br /> <br /> It could be as simple as the factions are getting uppity and doing a raid on the local city or in the case of a cross-faction coterie, then a mortal war erupting would make the kindred have to consider what to do. Do they assist the invaders, so the fighting is lessened and the collateral damaged minimized? Do they join the defense of the mortals to fight off the invaders? Alternatively, do they just kidnap dozens of humans and drag them off to their castle dungeons or underground warrens so that as the mortal world burns, they are well fed for the foreseeable future?<br /> <br /> If you can't find a common philosophy or a common enemy to motivate the group, then confront them with their common needs being put in jeopardy. They all need to feed, they all need a place to hide during the day, and they all need to be hidden from mortal society. As a benefit since these types of problems are complex and multi-layered then punching one bad guy in the face or using dominate won't make it go away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T17:42:31-08:00","id":1547355,"title":"","content":"You could always have a Justicar call a conclave there for some matter they want decided by as many vampires of the region as possible. Affected and interested parties could gather from different nearby cities.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat used to have a couple of annual festivals that would draw nomadic covens to the cities to participate. Though if you're playing V5 I don't know how feral packs that communicate by grunts and body language would get the invites out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T23:11:33-08:00","id":1547360,"title":"","content":"The obvious answer is the Jyhad<br /> Regardless of generation, clan, affiliation, or anything in theory all and every kindred are just pawns on someone else's chessboard<br /> It is totally in the realm of possibility an Ancient cashed in a few boons and moved his own pieces - in this case the kindred (or even other supernaturals and/or humans) in question - to one place for some unfathomable reason, including but not limited to because someone cashed in a boon of her own...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-31T01:39:31-08:00","id":1547363,"title":"","content":"How about '<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AWizardDidIt\" target=\"_blank\">A Wizard Did It</a>'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-31T02:20:37-08:00","id":1547365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547347-strangest-convergence?p=1547363#post1547363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about '<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AWizardDidIt\" target=\"_blank\">A Wizard Did It</a>'?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think even saying that it was all a big coincidence would be better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-31T15:11:20-08:00","id":1547385,"title":"","content":"Okay, in the end everything ends in the Jyhad, in that case help me with something else, maybe, give me your opinions.<br /> <br /> First, we have a Malkavian who is curiously proficient with oblivion and by curiously I mean that for him it is like a clan discipline. That said, what peculiarity would you think of for him?<br /> <br /> What reasons can you think of as to why a Brujah would embrace a wimp? The kind who can't assert himself, barely speaks, is a puppet of others and refuses to defend himself even when he is mistreated, including mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T04:02:00-08:00","id":1547415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547347-strangest-convergence?p=1547385#post1547385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, we have a Malkavian who is curiously proficient with oblivion and by curiously I mean that for him it is like a clan discipline. That said, what peculiarity would you think of for him?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Ankou</b>, the possibly 5th generation (many believe it to be a methuselah, grandchilde of Malkav and faithful servant of his sire) ancient terror that stalks the night and appears in Malkavians' dreams as a remorseless, lifeless monster that silently treads country roads with an ox-cart and scythe. If rumors can be trusted, it was birthed in the days when agriculture was a budding art, and was perhaps even slain and Embraced as a sacrifice to an earth-goddess.<br /> Where vampires, especially Malkavians, are known to disappear from their hunting grounds without a trace the Ankou been there and the after a disappearance, the Madness Network vibrates with whispers repeating &quot;Ankou&quot;.<br /> A few have said that Ankou is the first of the serial killers, or possibly their patron saint.<br /> It is the sort of equivalent to the Nictuku of the Malkavian and Mind's Eye Theatre introduced a bloodline connected to it, the Ananke.<br /> The Ananke believe that the secrets of the universe can be witnessed in a microcosm by scrutinizing the bodies of the recently dead. Wisdom can only be gained by savagely tearing into the corporeal, physically delving through the inner workings of each creature in creation<br /> The bloodline are said to have kept the ancient temples, where oracles performed haruspex (the art of divination through reading the entrails of a freshly killed animal) to read truths in blood.<br /> Ankou's connection to Death could explain that Malkvian's proficiency with Oblivion or even why basically have that as a Clan Discipline.<br /> Maybe he is the descendant of Ankou and inherited the connection to Death and the Underworld, fascination with death and the dead or even member of the Ananke bloodline not just could trace back her line to this enigmatic personification of Death<br /> Of course this would mean the Hecata are very interested in him (or really anyone with necromantic background, fascination with death, ancestry, the Underwourld, wraiths or simply someone disapered closed to him and blames the Malkav or tries to reach the Ancient thrugh him)<br /> If your Malkav is focusing on the &quot;Death aspect&quot; of Oblivion<br /> <br /> The other possible explanation is the Eater, also known as the Eater of Words<br /> This child of Malkav sustains himself not with blood, but with True Names, feeding over the platonic existences in order to incorporate other beings into himself.<br /> He began to consume words, believing it would make him wise again, and restore his sanity by eating names, biting chunks of reality itself free from the world and gulping them down \u2014 the first name he must surely have eaten was his own and he is forced to feast on other existences in a form of vampirism that is more severe than the curse levied by God on Caine.<br /> Some Malkavians say that the words he eats are gone forever - and so are the ideas. No one will never know what ideas are missing, because they are gone forever, and gone retroactively, so the Word-Eater is limiting the world to a smaller and more feeble reality all the time.<br /> This is Entropy, Oblivion in its purest form<br /> Devouring the Names would put the Wyrm itself to shame, and it is said Oblivion/Abyss is the Maw of the Wyrm itself anyway<br /> It is the primodial darkness that consumes and devours everything, swallowed by the Abyss it become forgotten<br /> The other side of Oblivion, if the Malkav focusin on the &quot;Abyssal, shadowy&quot; aspect of Oblivion<br /> The Malkav in question could be again the descendant of the Eater of Words and his proficiency with Oblivion (this aspect) is the manifestation of her heritage.<br /> Again would attract a lot of attention from everyone who is remotely aware of the important of True Names to anyone who is curious about the Abyss<br /> <br /> Now the Jyhad part<br /> Could be anything<br /> Maybe the Ankou and the Eater of Words are after the same thing (eg. the Malkavian) and/or would want to use her get rid of that thing<br /> But different method - one would want to erase it from existance, let the Abyss devour it and swallow it to be forever forgotten while the other would want it Dead, but not forgotten just dead, recycled back to the the cycle of life and death<br /> That thing could be anyone or anything really from person to an object, an idea or a sobject, really anything - and that thing could have a connection to other Vampires in one way or another, setting up a chain reaction for that auspicious meeting<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547347-strangest-convergence?p=1547385#post1547385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What reasons can you think of as to why a Brujah would embrace a wimp? The kind who can't assert himself, barely speaks, is a puppet of others and refuses to defend himself even when he is mistreated, including mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bThis is a bit easier to answer<br /> Maybe he saw the potential in the whimp, that pent up rage and wanted to help him and giving the Embrace is a &quot;Brujah therapy&quot;, truly wanted to help him to be who he could have been all along<br /> Or seeing the whimp's behavior made him so fustrated in his rage the Brujah killed him and punished him; if in life he was unable to face and harness his rage maybe in death he will be able to! Let him suffer for an eternity battlig the boiling blood of the Learned Clan and know true Passion!<br /> Or maybe - after all Learned Clan - it was just an experiment how the Embrace woudl effect such a person, maybe to understand the difference between Ilyes the original Progenitor and Troile, or maybe to understand and study something fundamental about the Human soul - or juts find a way to battle his own passion and rage by observin from the other way around how a whimp who was &quot;immune&quot; to the Rage handle it, and trace that back<br /> In any cases it could be very interesting or end very badly for the whimp in question, but with friends, family, coterie, etc. he could survive the first few nigfhts, taste the Frenzy, become familiar with the Beast and off to go!<br /> If you want to be really a bit sadistic DM give him a nasty Beast, a sentinent one!<br /> If you want to reflect that with Falws:<br /> <br /> The DA Flaw, Face of the Beast (2pt. Flaw) - The Beast Within emerges in times of hunger or stress, twisting your visage into a monstrous caricature of human form.<br /> And<br /> The Beast in the Mirror (1 or 2pt. Flaw) Flaw - Whenever you stare into a reflective surface, you see your Beast leering back at you.<br /> <br /> are two flaws that would make it especially nasty! Give him a P'o or Shadow-like Beast that whisper to him, or a mild insanity and have him to be like Gollum, battling his passinate raging Beast!<br /> Pair this with Demon-hounded (1 to 4pt. Flaw) - A demon from below has taken a special interest in you (in this case via the Beast, giving it voice and sentinence) and your Brujah whimp will have a hell of a ride!<br /> Or just give him this as a &quot;free gift of falws&quot; <br /> <br /> Or staying on the Jyhad part, a &quot;My Fair Lady&quot; kind of situation between two Brujah (or the Brujah or anyone else really)<br /> <br /> &quot;Not even you could make a proper Brujah out of *that* one...&quot;<br /> &quot;Okay, it is a bet!&quot;<br /> <br /> And you have the boons and things in motion again\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-