oodline are said to have kept the ancient temples, where oracles performed haruspex (the art of divination through reading the entrails of a freshly killed animal) to read truths in blood.<br /> Ankou's connection to Death could explain that Malkvian's proficiency with Oblivion or even why basically have that as a Clan Discipline.<br /> Maybe he is the descendant of Ankou and inherited the connection to Death and the Underworld, fascination with death and the dead or even member of the Ananke bloodline not just could trace back her line to this enigmatic personification of Death<br /> Of course this would mean the Hecata are very interested in him (or really anyone with necromantic background, fascination with death, ancestry, the Underwourld, wraiths or simply someone disapered closed to him and blames the Malkav or tries to reach the Ancient thrugh him)<br /> If your Malkav is focusing on the &quot;Death aspect&quot; of Oblivion<br /> <br /> The other possible explanation is the Eater, also known as the Eater of Words<br /> This child of Malkav sustains himself not with blood, but with True Names, feeding over the platonic existences in order to incorporate other beings into himself.<br /> He began to consume words, believing it would make him wise again, and restore his sanity by eating names, biting chunks of reality itself free from the world and gulping them down \u2014 the first name he must surely have eaten was his own and he is forced to feast on other existences in a form of vampirism that is more severe than the curse levied by God on Caine.<br /> Some Malkavians say that the words he eats are gone forever - and so are the ideas. No one will never know what ideas are missing, because they are gone forever, and gone retroactively, so the Word-Eater is limiting the world to a smaller and more feeble reality all the time.<br /> This is Entropy, Oblivion in its purest form<br /> Devouring the Names would put the Wyrm itself to shame, and it is said Oblivion/Abyss is the Maw of the Wyrm itself anyway<br /> It is the primodial darkness that consumes and devours everything, swallowed by the Abyss it become forgotten<br /> The other side of Oblivion, if the Malkav focusin on the &quot;Abyssal, shadowy&quot; aspect of Oblivion<br /> The Malkav in question could be again the descendant of the Eater of Words and his proficiency with Oblivion (this aspect) is the manifestation of her heritage.<br /> Again would attract a lot of attention from everyone who is remotely aware of the important of True Names to anyone who is curious about the Abyss<br /> <br /> Now the Jyhad part<br /> Could be anything<br /> Maybe the Ankou and the Eater of Words are after the same thing (eg. the Malkavian) and/or would want to use her get rid of that thing<br /> But different method - one would want to erase it from existance, let the Abyss devour it and swallow it to be forever forgotten while the other would want it Dead, but not forgotten just dead, recycled back to the the cycle of life and death<br /> That thing could be anyone or anything really from person to an object, an idea or a sobject, really anything - and that thing could have a connection to other Vampires in one way or another, setting up a chain reaction for that auspicious meeting</div> </div> </div> </div>Look... you managed to accidentally help me with another question, ironically. As for the Malkavian, those are good ideas to think about and could explain his affinity, but I thought of something more down to earth for his disturbance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547347-strangest-convergence?p=1547415#post1547415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis is a bit easier to answer<br /> Maybe he saw the potential in the whimp, that pent up rage and wanted to help him and giving the Embrace is a &quot;Brujah therapy&quot;, truly wanted to help him to be who he could have been all along<br /> Or seeing the whimp's behavior made him so fustrated in his rage the Brujah killed him and punished him; if in life he was unable to face and harness his rage maybe in death he will be able to! Let him suffer for an eternity battlig the boiling blood of the Learned Clan and know true Passion!<br /> Or maybe - after all Learned Clan - it was just an experiment how the Embrace woudl effect such a person, maybe to understand the difference between Ilyes the original Progenitor and Troile, or maybe to understand and study something fundamental about the Human soul - or juts find a way to battle his own passion and rage by observin from the other way around how a whimp who was &quot;immune&quot; to the Rage handle it, and trace that back<br /> In any cases it could be very interesting or end very badly for the whimp in question, but with friends, family, coterie, etc. he could survive the first few nigfhts, taste the Frenzy, become familiar with the Beast and off to go!<br /> If you want to be really a bit sadistic DM give him a nasty Beast, a sentinent one!<br /> If you want to reflect that with Falws:<br /> <br /> The DA Flaw, Face of the Beast (2pt. Flaw) - The Beast Within emerges in times of hunger or stress, twisting your visage into a monstrous caricature of human form.<br /> And<br /> The Beast in the Mirror (1 or 2pt. Flaw) Flaw - Whenever you stare into a reflective surface, you see your Beast leering back at you.<br /> <br /> are two flaws that would make it especially nasty! Give him a P'o or Shadow-like Beast that whisper to him, or a mild insanity and have him to be like Gollum, battling his passinate raging Beast!<br /> Pair this with Demon-hounded (1 to 4pt. Flaw) - A demon from below has taken a special interest in you (in this case via the Beast, giving it voice and sentinence) and your Brujah whimp will have a hell of a ride!<br /> Or just give him this as a &quot;free gift of falws&quot;<br /> <br /> Or staying on the Jyhad part, a &quot;My Fair Lady&quot; kind of situation between two Brujah (or the Brujah or anyone else really)<br /> <br /> &quot;Not even you could make a proper Brujah out of *that* one...&quot;<br /> &quot;Okay, it is a bet!&quot;<br /> <br /> And you have the boons and things in motion again\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That might actually work. But explain to me, to what extent could the beast change its appearance at the time of frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T08:14:20-08:00","id":1547422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547347-strangest-convergence?p=1547420#post1547420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look... you managed to accidentally help me with another question, ironically. As for the Malkavian, those are good ideas to think about and could explain his affinity, but I thought of something more down to earth for his disturbance.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Oblivion I think nothing is down to the earth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547347-strangest-convergence?p=1547420#post1547420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might actually work. But explain to me, to what extent could the beast change its appearance at the time of frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is up to the Storyteller basically<br /> From the Dr. Jekyll \u00e9s Mr. Hyde to the full blown dark monster that would pass as a demon or a Garou, or like a Banner and Hulk transformation - the meek and quiet whimp when in frenzy transforms a buff alpha chad jock and grows, could crush skulls in his palm. Since possibly the whimp in question a virgin throw in some pent up sexual fustration and libido with the passion of the dead and let him loose in the neighborhood<br /> <br /> Really it is up to you<br /> Transofrm or twist, sudden pale skin, sharp fangs, sneering like a fearl beast, red glowing eyes without puppils, claws - whatever you find in other disciplines (especially Protean) that &quot;borrows a trait of the Beast&quot; arew fair play and slap them on<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T15:43:43-08:00","id":1547435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547347-strangest-convergence?p=1547385#post1547385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, in the end everything ends in the Jyhad, in that case help me with something else, maybe, give me your opinions.<br /> <br /> First, we have a Malkavian who is curiously proficient with oblivion and by curiously I mean that for him it is like a clan discipline. That said, what peculiarity would you think of for him?<br /> <br /> What reasons can you think of as to why a Brujah would embrace a wimp? The kind who can't assert himself, barely speaks, is a puppet of others and refuses to defend himself even when he is mistreated, including mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Brujah there could be any reasons as Brujah are people primarily and not mindless extensions of the Clan Hive Mind.<br /> <br /> As such maybe the whimp stood up for himself at one time when a Brujah was nearby to witness it?<br /> <br /> Maybe the Brujah got so infurated that he decided the whimp needed to toughen up, or that being a little tougher was what the whimp needed to start to stand up for himself?<br /> <br /> Not all Embraces are made after a decade of cold calculations and investigation of the candidate but many of them, especially made by younger Cainites, seems to be done on impulse or on a whim. This should not be underestimated in how that brings unorthodox members into any Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}